                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "the animations and character designs are very B-movie styled like many other of microids works\nthe story isn't actually about nessie but rather about the submarine below the \"monster\"\nand other things about crystals, a trisket, and destroying england\n\nthe movement seems pretty good, the camera moves with the cursor and the cursor will change whenever it hovers over items of note, the icons are pretty clear about if you are the correct things or not, and it will be clear about what items you can and can't combine\noverall, there are only a few actual puzzles and they stick out strangely in this game of walking, and improper use of roman numerals as well\n\nthere can still be a good bit of searching as there are plenty of places to explore even if you can't go into most of them, but the game can still feel like a maze since the rooms with no more value stay open for the most part \n\nthe game is fine, but wasn't of much note, didn't feel like the time was well spent walking around",
